1
00:00:01,198 --> 00:00:04,592
(A Fated Meeting)

2
00:00:04,617 --> 00:00:05,887
Nice to see you all.

3
00:00:06,910 --> 00:00:08,149
- Nice to see you. - Oh, my.

4
00:00:08,150 --> 00:00:10,319
Seriously. Our show is full of youthful faces, isn't it?

5
00:00:10,320 --> 00:00:12,049
- Yes. - It's giving off a college vibe.

6
00:00:12,050 --> 00:00:13,050
- What? - Stop it, Hyun Moo.

7
00:00:13,051 --> 00:00:14,149
A college vibe...

8
00:00:14,150 --> 00:00:15,819
That's why I dressed like a college student.

9
00:00:15,820 --> 00:00:17,389
- For today's episode? - To look fresh.

10
00:00:17,390 --> 00:00:18,419
- To look fresh. - Yes.

11
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:19,629
- That's your college student look? - Right.

12
00:00:19,630 --> 00:00:21,230
(A fresh college student look)

13
00:00:22,130 --> 00:00:23,930
I know I said "college student."

14
00:00:24,160 --> 00:00:26,830
But I do look old. Like a soldier from the barracks, right?

15
00:00:27,730 --> 00:00:28,870
Very much.

16
00:00:29,770 --> 00:00:31,099
Considering the ranks,

17
00:00:31,100 --> 00:00:33,839
Kian84's rank is the one to be feared the most.

18
00:00:33,840 --> 00:00:35,769
- I'm the powerless sergeant. - He has the actual power.

19
00:00:35,770 --> 00:00:38,040
- You'd have no real power. - I'd have no real power.

20
00:00:38,210 --> 00:00:40,349
If you have a problem, talk to me first.

21
00:00:40,350 --> 00:00:41,909
Okay. That sounds great.

22
00:00:41,910 --> 00:00:43,620
Don't let Hyun Moo hear it.

23
00:00:44,050 --> 00:00:45,520
- I'm a toothless tiger. - Right.

24
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:47,719
- Have we all met each other before? - No.

25
00:00:47,720 --> 00:00:49,636
- Whom have you not met before? - It's my first time...

26
00:00:49,660 --> 00:00:51,619
- meeting Dowoon today. - Really?

27
00:00:51,620 --> 00:00:52,620
- We haven't met before. - Same here.

28
00:00:52,621 --> 00:00:53,689
- MINHO is older. - We haven't met either.

29
00:00:53,690 --> 00:00:55,389
- Right. - You two are the same age.

30
00:00:55,390 --> 00:00:57,306
- Exactly. We're the same age. - Yes. You should be friends.

31
00:00:57,330 --> 00:00:58,459
- Nice to meet you. - Yes.

32
00:00:58,460 --> 00:01:00,069
Drop the honorifics since you're the same age.

33
00:01:00,070 --> 00:01:02,630
You have to do what the powerful member says.

34
00:01:02,970 --> 00:01:04,170
That's the rule.

35
00:01:04,440 --> 00:01:06,516
- Right. You were both born in 1995. - That's right.

36
00:01:06,540 --> 00:01:08,639
- You love fishing, Dowoon. - That's right.

37
00:01:08,640 --> 00:01:10,740
I used to love fishing too.

38
00:01:10,810 --> 00:01:12,340
Dowoon can catch fish.

39
00:01:12,780 --> 00:01:14,249
Then Ji Hyeon can fillet them.

40
00:01:14,250 --> 00:01:15,250
- That's right. - Yes.

41
00:01:15,250 --> 00:01:16,250
- That's right. - Dowoon...

42
00:01:16,251 --> 00:01:17,619
- Let's go fishing together. - Yes.

43
00:01:17,620 --> 00:01:18,749
- Sounds good. I'd love to. - Yes.

44
00:01:18,750 --> 00:01:22,350
Now, you guys have to lead the show.

45
00:01:23,820 --> 00:01:25,989
- You must lead the show. - Right.

46
00:01:25,990 --> 00:01:27,330
You guys have a lot to do.

47
00:01:28,190 --> 00:01:29,629
That's because we're old news.

48
00:01:29,630 --> 00:01:30,760
(We got it, sir!)

49
00:01:31,360 --> 00:01:32,699
(Into the Winter)

50
00:01:32,700 --> 00:01:33,900
"Into the Winter."

51
00:01:35,500 --> 00:01:37,940
(Groaning)

52
00:01:38,800 --> 00:01:41,039
(Current time, 5:20am)

53
00:01:41,040 --> 00:01:42,240
That's way too early.

54
00:01:44,980 --> 00:01:46,250
What's taking him so long?

55
00:01:48,810 --> 00:01:49,919
It's the crack of dawn.

56
00:01:49,920 --> 00:01:52,240
(What's he doing at Mount Cheonggye at the crack of dawn?)

57
00:01:53,090 --> 00:01:54,150
It's freezing.

58
00:01:56,620 --> 00:01:57,790
What's the temperature at?

59
00:02:00,490 --> 00:02:02,060
It's at minus 10°C. Oh, my.

60
00:02:02,630 --> 00:02:04,429
(Weather, minus 10°C)

61
00:02:04,430 --> 00:02:06,150
But the apparent temperature is minus 11°C.

62
00:02:06,400 --> 00:02:07,929
The temperature this morning dropped over 10°C...

63
00:02:07,930 --> 00:02:10,070
- since yesterday. - It was the biggest cold wave.

64
00:02:10,200 --> 00:02:13,040
The apparent temperature will go as low as minus 20°C.

65
00:02:13,370 --> 00:02:15,269
- That's way too cold to be out. - Minus 20°C?

66
00:02:15,270 --> 00:02:16,709
- It was really cold a few days ago. - Yes.

67
00:02:16,710 --> 00:02:18,040
It wasn't as bad the day before.

68
00:02:18,210 --> 00:02:21,280
Then it got extremely cold in the morning.

69
00:02:21,980 --> 00:02:23,620
- Kian84. - Hey.

70
00:02:25,080 --> 00:02:26,720
- Kian84. - Hey.

71
00:02:27,450 --> 00:02:28,620
Hey, Dowoon.

72
00:02:29,220 --> 00:02:30,719
- Kian84. - Hey.

73
00:02:30,720 --> 00:02:31,720
It's Dowoon.

74
00:02:31,721 --> 00:02:33,281
(He meets Dowoon early in the morning.)

75
00:02:34,160 --> 00:02:35,559
- Did you sleep well? - What?

76
00:02:35,560 --> 00:02:36,630
This year...

77
00:02:37,400 --> 00:02:39,100
On the New Year's Day,

78
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:40,699
I didn't get to see the sunrise.

79
00:02:40,700 --> 00:02:44,100
But I still wanted to see it in the beginning of the year.

80
00:02:44,640 --> 00:02:46,440
I invited Dowoon of DAY6.

81
00:02:46,770 --> 00:02:48,710
I decided to hike with Dowoon.

82
00:02:48,840 --> 00:02:50,979
Surprisingly, at the bazaar,

83
00:02:50,980 --> 00:02:54,010
all the items he chose were mine.

84
00:02:54,480 --> 00:02:56,450
(This fishing rod looks great.)

85
00:02:56,880 --> 00:02:58,020
You guys clicked well.

86
00:02:58,120 --> 00:02:59,219
That's a cute boyfriend look.

87
00:02:59,220 --> 00:03:01,389
(He connects especially well with Dowoon.)

88
00:03:01,390 --> 00:03:02,749
We both like fishing.

89
00:03:02,750 --> 00:03:04,059
We had a lot in common.

90
00:03:04,060 --> 00:03:07,189
Exercising is the best way for guys to bond.

91
00:03:07,190 --> 00:03:10,200
I wanted us to break a good sweat and get some exercise together.

92
00:03:10,730 --> 00:03:13,300
I thought that always brought guys closer.

93
00:03:13,430 --> 00:03:15,230
On top of that, he likes hiking too.

94
00:03:15,570 --> 00:03:16,639
So we decided to go together.

95
00:03:16,640 --> 00:03:18,276
Besides, Mount Cheonggye has good energy.

96
00:03:18,300 --> 00:03:19,669
When I bought clothes from him,

97
00:03:19,670 --> 00:03:21,410
he and I seemed to click well.

98
00:03:21,740 --> 00:03:25,080
I thought, "This guy and I might get along well."

99
00:03:25,210 --> 00:03:27,610
So I asked him to go hiking with me.

100
00:03:28,680 --> 00:03:30,156
(Kian84 and Dowoon came to get good energy.)

101
00:03:30,180 --> 00:03:32,779
- Did you get some sleep? - I only slept for three hours.

102
00:03:32,780 --> 00:03:33,849
Let's go.

103
00:03:33,850 --> 00:03:35,850
- Why didn't you invite me? - What?

104
00:03:36,120 --> 00:03:38,160
- Why didn't you invite me? - What?

105
00:03:39,260 --> 00:03:40,929
That's the thing about me.

106
00:03:40,930 --> 00:03:42,970
I can't interact with more than two people at once.

107
00:03:43,330 --> 00:03:44,599
I can't multitask.

108
00:03:44,600 --> 00:03:47,230
- Is he your new favorite now? - I wouldn't say that.

109
00:03:47,600 --> 00:03:49,530
I can't talk to only one person at a time.

110
00:03:49,940 --> 00:03:51,770
You might've been neglected had you come.

111
00:03:52,270 --> 00:03:54,740
- I'll do better. - Gosh, no.

112
00:03:55,040 --> 00:03:57,309
- Gosh, Ji Hyeon is so cute. - Oh, no.

113
00:03:57,310 --> 00:03:59,140
- Kian84 is the leader. - What?

114
00:03:59,240 --> 00:04:00,910
Is it my time now?

115
00:04:01,780 --> 00:04:04,280
(Irresistible84 continues to draw attention from men.)

116
00:04:04,980 --> 00:04:07,189
No, don't be disappointed. You two should be friends.

117
00:04:07,190 --> 00:04:08,220
- Sounds good. - Sure.

118
00:04:08,890 --> 00:04:10,820
(He begins hiking with his new guy.)

119
00:04:11,190 --> 00:04:12,520
Do you go hiking often?

120
00:04:13,560 --> 00:04:14,659
- Me? - Yes.

121
00:04:14,660 --> 00:04:15,660
I sometimes go hiking.

122
00:04:15,661 --> 00:04:18,060
I know that you do a lot of marathons.

123
00:04:18,300 --> 00:04:19,329
- But these days, - Yes.

124
00:04:19,330 --> 00:04:20,929
I run only 10km.

125
00:04:20,930 --> 00:04:22,100
- Only 10km? - Yes.

126
00:04:23,400 --> 00:04:25,570
Do you like staying active?

127
00:04:25,940 --> 00:04:28,139
I keep exercising because I'm getting older.

128
00:04:28,140 --> 00:04:29,339
I didn't exercise much when I was your age.

129
00:04:29,340 --> 00:04:30,409
I was so full of energy then.

130
00:04:30,410 --> 00:04:32,379
- How old are you? - I'm 32 years old now.

131
00:04:32,380 --> 00:04:34,110
- You're 32? My gosh. - Yes.

132
00:04:34,780 --> 00:04:36,349
That's why I exercise a lot now.

133
00:04:36,350 --> 00:04:37,670
You must have so much energy now.

134
00:04:38,320 --> 00:04:39,579
So you exercise a lot?

135
00:04:39,580 --> 00:04:40,890
I box.

136
00:04:42,350 --> 00:04:44,020
I need to be able to protect myself.

137
00:04:44,490 --> 00:04:45,890
Ji Hyeon boxes too.

138
00:04:46,260 --> 00:04:47,330
- You box too. - Yes.

139
00:04:48,760 --> 00:04:50,999
He even participated in a boxing match.

140
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:52,559
- Really? - No, I didn't.

141
00:04:52,560 --> 00:04:53,629
He even participated in a boxing match.

142
00:04:53,630 --> 00:04:55,230
- Really? - No, I didn't.

143
00:04:55,500 --> 00:04:56,869
- You didn't? - When...

144
00:04:56,870 --> 00:04:58,099
- You didn't? - I didn't.

145
00:04:58,100 --> 00:05:01,070
- What? You need to be sure. - Ji Hyeon, do a match then.

146
00:05:01,410 --> 00:05:04,209
- I thought you did five matches. - What are you talking about?

147
00:05:04,210 --> 00:05:06,510
I even thought you won the match.

148
00:05:06,880 --> 00:05:08,980
- What on earth? - How did the misinformation start?

149
00:05:10,280 --> 00:05:12,250
- Right? - Are you planning to fight a match?

150
00:05:12,420 --> 00:05:14,249
- No. I stopped boxing now. - I see.

151
00:05:14,250 --> 00:05:15,489
- But you used to box? - Yes.

152
00:05:15,490 --> 00:05:16,919
- Show him your jabs. - How many years...

153
00:05:16,920 --> 00:05:17,960
I...

154
00:05:18,820 --> 00:05:20,190
You're going to show us?

155
00:05:20,560 --> 00:05:21,960
- He's going to show us? - Show us.

156
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:28,969
(His shadowboxing cuts through the air.)

157
00:05:28,970 --> 00:05:31,040
(Impressed)

158
00:05:33,410 --> 00:05:34,840
(Amazed)

159
00:05:35,010 --> 00:05:36,879
It does feel like we're in the military, talking about this.

160
00:05:36,880 --> 00:05:37,940
(A dull vibe)

161
00:05:38,540 --> 00:05:40,150
This feels like reserve training.

162
00:05:40,710 --> 00:05:42,380
When will you throw me a discharge party?

163
00:05:42,710 --> 00:05:45,190
- Okay. We'll throw you a party. - I got the patches stitched.

164
00:05:46,120 --> 00:05:48,119
Are you wearing the clothes you bought that day?

165
00:05:48,120 --> 00:05:50,190
- The clothes look so cute. - Yes?

166
00:05:50,760 --> 00:05:53,229
I'm not lying. I mean it. I actually wore it.

167
00:05:53,230 --> 00:05:54,289
- Really? - I wore it 2 or 3 times.

168
00:05:54,290 --> 00:05:55,360
Yes.

169
00:05:55,690 --> 00:05:58,230
I've never hiked Mount Cheonggye at this hour.

170
00:05:58,830 --> 00:06:00,830
- It's my 1st time. - It's my 1st time too.

171
00:06:01,770 --> 00:06:03,670
It's my first time hiking Mount Cheonggye.

172
00:06:04,270 --> 00:06:06,300
- Which way do we have to go? - We...

173
00:06:06,610 --> 00:06:07,610
Yes.

174
00:06:07,611 --> 00:06:09,239
We should go toward Maebong Peak. There.

175
00:06:09,240 --> 00:06:11,340
- The elevation is about 580m. - That's quite high.

176
00:06:11,640 --> 00:06:14,250
Kian84, do you often hike Mount Cheonggye?

177
00:06:14,380 --> 00:06:17,150
That's the closest mountain from my place.

178
00:06:17,480 --> 00:06:20,750
I go there at least 2 or 3 times a year.

179
00:06:21,420 --> 00:06:22,820
- Maebong Peak looks great. - Okay.

180
00:06:23,320 --> 00:06:24,390
It takes two hours.

181
00:06:25,520 --> 00:06:26,829
(The Maebong Course takes 2 hours.)

182
00:06:26,830 --> 00:06:28,630
The sun will rise before they reach the peak.

183
00:06:28,890 --> 00:06:31,000
- It's 5:30am now. - It's 5:30am now.

184
00:06:31,400 --> 00:06:32,960
Let me check the sunrise time.

185
00:06:33,900 --> 00:06:36,029
Hey, the sun will rise at 7:40am.

186
00:06:36,030 --> 00:06:37,769
- Really? It will be perfect then. - Yes.

187
00:06:37,770 --> 00:06:39,069
- We have exactly 2 hours. - We have exactly 2 hours.

188
00:06:39,070 --> 00:06:40,240
- We must hurry. - Let's go.

189
00:06:40,310 --> 00:06:41,370
Yes.

190
00:06:41,510 --> 00:06:43,310
- There's a slight incline. - What?

191
00:06:43,840 --> 00:06:45,280
- There's a slight incline. - Yes.

192
00:06:45,840 --> 00:06:47,150
Hey. This is nice, though.

193
00:06:47,910 --> 00:06:50,320
- Isn't it nice? - I love it.

194
00:06:51,150 --> 00:06:53,550
I can tell Dowoon is a positive, cheerful person.

195
00:06:54,050 --> 00:06:56,620
(Hiking to the peak)

196
00:06:58,560 --> 00:06:59,860
It's really dark.

197
00:07:00,490 --> 00:07:02,560
It's dark. Let me turn on the lantern.

198
00:07:02,830 --> 00:07:04,030
- People here... - Yes.

199
00:07:05,160 --> 00:07:06,829
He brought a lantern.

200
00:07:06,830 --> 00:07:09,200
There aren't any lamps.

201
00:07:09,600 --> 00:07:10,839
Gosh, you can see my breath.

202
00:07:10,840 --> 00:07:12,040
(Gosh, you can see my breath.)

203
00:07:12,440 --> 00:07:13,720
Let's put on the climbing irons.

204
00:07:13,840 --> 00:07:16,070
- I brought a pair for you too. - Thank you.

205
00:07:16,780 --> 00:07:17,839
These are nice.

206
00:07:17,840 --> 00:07:21,510
(Dowoon brought two pairs of climbing irons.)

207
00:07:22,350 --> 00:07:23,420
Thank you for this.

208
00:07:23,950 --> 00:07:25,720
- Are you all set? - Yes, I'm all set.

209
00:07:27,350 --> 00:07:29,550
Without the lantern, you can't see anything.

210
00:07:30,090 --> 00:07:31,850
It will be dangerous without climbing irons.

211
00:07:37,030 --> 00:07:38,360
Gosh, it's a bit spooky here.

212
00:07:39,260 --> 00:07:40,430
It's scary.

213
00:07:40,900 --> 00:07:42,530
- It's a horror movie. - It's scary.

214
00:07:42,800 --> 00:07:44,739
- Like we're walking into death. - Right. I thought so too.

215
00:07:44,740 --> 00:07:45,899
(The two of them head into the pitch-black darkness.)

216
00:07:45,900 --> 00:07:48,220
- Like we're walking into death. - It does feel like that.

217
00:07:49,140 --> 00:07:50,740
Gosh, look how dark it is.

218
00:07:51,810 --> 00:07:54,180
- It reminds me of "Mystery Squad." - Yes.

219
00:07:57,850 --> 00:07:59,530
This is a scene straight out of "Gonjiam."

220
00:08:00,790 --> 00:08:02,549
- My gosh. - Why is there a red light?

221
00:08:02,550 --> 00:08:04,119
- Let's hurry. This is creepy. - This is so scary.

222
00:08:04,120 --> 00:08:05,920
- That was sudden. - This is scary.

223
00:08:06,360 --> 00:08:07,889
It was really creepy with the red light.

224
00:08:07,890 --> 00:08:09,230
(Their hike gets spookier.)

225
00:08:09,760 --> 00:08:10,999
You can't watch horror movies either?

226
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:12,459
Me? I can watch them with friends.

227
00:08:12,460 --> 00:08:13,540
(I can't watch them alone.)

228
00:08:13,800 --> 00:08:15,899
I don't like movies that are too extreme.

229
00:08:15,900 --> 00:08:17,840
- But they're fun to watch. - Sure. But...

230
00:08:19,740 --> 00:08:20,970
My gosh. Hello.

231
00:08:22,810 --> 00:08:23,839
- What? - My goodness.

232
00:08:23,840 --> 00:08:25,010
- Hello. - Who's that?

233
00:08:25,180 --> 00:08:26,500
- I was so startled. - Seriously.

234
00:08:26,910 --> 00:08:29,149
- It's like a Japanese horror movie. - What's this?

235
00:08:29,150 --> 00:08:30,419
- Here's the thing. - I got so startled.

236
00:08:30,420 --> 00:08:32,380
I couldn't see a thing. It was pitch-dark.

237
00:08:32,550 --> 00:08:34,619
- She talked to us out of the blue. - Gosh.

238
00:08:34,620 --> 00:08:35,719
- She was like, "Hey, Kian84." - Then...

239
00:08:35,720 --> 00:08:38,120
- she must've started at 3am. - Exactly.

240
00:08:38,260 --> 00:08:39,666
- She's going down now. - She's all alone too.

241
00:08:39,690 --> 00:08:41,429
- She didn't have a lantern. - Right.

242
00:08:41,430 --> 00:08:42,959
- That makes no sense. - She probably used her phone light.

243
00:08:42,960 --> 00:08:44,506
- The flashlight from her phone. - Really?

244
00:08:44,530 --> 00:08:47,170
It looked like she came for her morning prayer.

245
00:08:47,230 --> 00:08:48,370
That's crazy.

246
00:08:50,800 --> 00:08:52,000
That's so scary. My gosh.

247
00:08:52,600 --> 00:08:53,740
- Hello. - She startled me.

248
00:08:54,010 --> 00:08:57,210
I think Kian84 walked past her because he was scared.

249
00:08:57,510 --> 00:08:58,939
- Right? - She was like, "What?"

250
00:08:58,940 --> 00:09:00,149
I was flustered too.

251
00:09:00,150 --> 00:09:01,509
- Safe hiking. - So we walked past each other.

252
00:09:01,510 --> 00:09:03,009
I would've been startled too.

253
00:09:03,010 --> 00:09:04,796
(The unexpected encounter flusters them both.)

254
00:09:04,820 --> 00:09:06,419
- I... - At night...

255
00:09:06,420 --> 00:09:07,750
I could never do this alone.

256
00:09:08,420 --> 00:09:10,689
It looks like she's in special forces or something.

257
00:09:10,690 --> 00:09:12,810
(It looks like she's in special forces or something.)

258
00:09:13,990 --> 00:09:15,930
Gosh, why is it so long and scary?

259
00:09:16,490 --> 00:09:18,129
- This is scary, right? - Right.

260
00:09:18,130 --> 00:09:19,229
(Following the path the special agent must have walked)

261
00:09:19,230 --> 00:09:20,729
You couldn't have hiked without the light.

262
00:09:20,730 --> 00:09:22,530
Right. The lantern was a must.

263
00:09:23,900 --> 00:09:25,739
- Let's go fishing sometime. - What?

264
00:09:25,740 --> 00:09:27,860
- Let's go fishing sometime. - Yes, let's go fishing.

265
00:09:27,970 --> 00:09:29,040
March or April?

266
00:09:29,210 --> 00:09:32,710
March or April? Then there aren't a lot of boats on the west coast.

267
00:09:33,110 --> 00:09:34,456
Do you want to fish in the freshwater?

268
00:09:34,480 --> 00:09:36,819
- That sounds great. - I like freshwater fishing.

269
00:09:36,820 --> 00:09:38,700
- Kian84, I... - My face won't be on TV, right?

270
00:09:38,880 --> 00:09:40,449
Dowoon. It looks like you're up on stage.

271
00:09:40,450 --> 00:09:42,170
- You have the lantern on your head. - Yes.

272
00:09:42,550 --> 00:09:44,359
- His face won't be on TV today. - Right.

273
00:09:44,360 --> 00:09:46,760
- It's like he's at a concert. - His face is really glowing.

274
00:09:46,790 --> 00:09:49,460
- His face... - His handsome face is blinding me.

275
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:51,280
We've only heard of such a face.

276
00:09:54,130 --> 00:09:55,970
- There's an incline. - What?

277
00:09:56,500 --> 00:09:58,000
- There's an incline. - Yes.

278
00:09:59,200 --> 00:10:01,070
(Panting)

279
00:10:01,540 --> 00:10:02,870
They're getting tired.

280
00:10:05,340 --> 00:10:08,209
(In no time, )

281
00:10:08,210 --> 00:10:10,249
(only their sounds of breathing and footsteps are heard.)

282
00:10:10,250 --> 00:10:12,320
Both of them started to get quiet.

283
00:10:12,450 --> 00:10:13,550
You know how it feels.

284
00:10:13,820 --> 00:10:15,580
I'd get annoyed when people talk to me then.

285
00:10:17,720 --> 00:10:19,789
(Walking up)

286
00:10:19,790 --> 00:10:20,930
Gosh, it's freezing.

287
00:10:24,900 --> 00:10:26,429
(The temperature drops sharply as they hike up.)

288
00:10:26,430 --> 00:10:28,330
You guys went on the coldest day.

289
00:10:28,470 --> 00:10:30,270
Right. And at the coldest hour too.

290
00:10:30,440 --> 00:10:32,399
My ears were about to freeze off.

291
00:10:32,400 --> 00:10:33,609
Yes. It'd feel like they'd tear off.

292
00:10:33,610 --> 00:10:35,090
(The current temperature, minus 14°C)

293
00:10:36,140 --> 00:10:37,310
Aren't your ears cold?

294
00:10:37,510 --> 00:10:39,539
- My ears? - Yes. Mine are about to freeze off.

295
00:10:39,540 --> 00:10:40,649
Right.

296
00:10:40,650 --> 00:10:42,210
I should've brought a hoodie.

297
00:10:42,880 --> 00:10:44,179
- You're not wearing a hoodie. - Right.

298
00:10:44,180 --> 00:10:46,419
Exactly. They didn't bring any proper gear.

299
00:10:46,420 --> 00:10:48,189
- Right. - You should've worn earmuffs.

300
00:10:48,190 --> 00:10:49,190
Seriously.

301
00:10:49,191 --> 00:10:51,660
In my eyes, you two didn't dress properly for hiking.

302
00:10:51,890 --> 00:10:54,189
I do admit that I treated the hiking trip lightly.

303
00:10:54,190 --> 00:10:55,190
You thought it'd be easy like hiking a hill?

304
00:10:55,191 --> 00:10:56,799
Yes, that's what I thought.

305
00:10:56,800 --> 00:10:58,059
- I didn't know it'd be that cold. - It's tough.

306
00:10:58,060 --> 00:11:00,169
- You'd also sweat on your way up. - Right.

307
00:11:00,170 --> 00:11:01,469
You must wear several thin layers...

308
00:11:01,470 --> 00:11:02,769
- of clothing. - Right.

309
00:11:02,770 --> 00:11:05,640
If you only wear one padded jacket, it'd get too hot later.

310
00:11:05,770 --> 00:11:07,109
- You'd be cold if you took it off. - Right.

311
00:11:07,110 --> 00:11:08,210
That'd be uncomfortable.

312
00:11:09,610 --> 00:11:11,439
- You should've covered your ears, - Right.

313
00:11:11,440 --> 00:11:12,609
- your neck, and your hands. - Yes.

314
00:11:12,610 --> 00:11:15,509
Covering up those places would have kept you warm.

315
00:11:15,510 --> 00:11:17,070
(Their feet are beginning to get numb.)

316
00:11:20,490 --> 00:11:21,589
(Looking flushed)

317
00:11:21,590 --> 00:11:23,219
You look so cold, Kian84.

318
00:11:23,220 --> 00:11:24,900
It looks like I drank two bottles of soju.

319
00:11:25,790 --> 00:11:26,960
You look drunk.

320
00:11:27,390 --> 00:11:29,559
- Even your eyes are out of focus. - Definitely.

321
00:11:29,560 --> 00:11:30,860
(Looking drunk)

322
00:11:32,130 --> 00:11:34,870
(His face gets puffy from the biting cold.)

323
00:11:35,930 --> 00:11:37,169
I think we're halfway there.

324
00:11:37,170 --> 00:11:39,340
(I think we're halfway there.)

325
00:11:40,770 --> 00:11:43,680
- We can slow down. - Sure. Let's go. I can do it.

326
00:11:43,980 --> 00:11:46,180
Let's go. I can do it.

327
00:11:46,710 --> 00:11:47,979
Your body is going numb.

328
00:11:47,980 --> 00:11:49,940
(Even his mouth is getting numb due to the cold.)

329
00:11:51,020 --> 00:11:52,150
My gosh.

330
00:11:53,350 --> 00:11:55,120
- Goodness. - Oh, my.

331
00:11:57,190 --> 00:11:58,660
Darn it.

332
00:12:00,730 --> 00:12:03,430
(In the end, his inner thought slips out.)

333
00:12:03,830 --> 00:12:06,130
Gosh, why is it so high? We're not hiking the Himalayas.

334
00:12:07,300 --> 00:12:08,870
The mountain must've gone up.

335
00:12:09,830 --> 00:12:10,940
It's gotten taller.

336
00:12:14,540 --> 00:12:16,669
(Exhausted)

337
00:12:16,670 --> 00:12:18,579
It felt like I was getting punished then.

338
00:12:18,580 --> 00:12:21,350
I kept feeling the burn in my legs.

339
00:12:21,510 --> 00:12:24,020
Then there was nothing but darkness. I couldn't see a thing.

340
00:12:24,320 --> 00:12:26,650
It was so cold. It was just painful.

341
00:12:26,890 --> 00:12:28,350
- Right. - I bet.

342
00:12:28,650 --> 00:12:30,619
If they were cold even when they were sweating,

343
00:12:30,620 --> 00:12:31,860
it must've been extremely cold.

344
00:12:31,920 --> 00:12:34,559
Actually, at that time, I kind of regretted deciding to hike.

345
00:12:34,560 --> 00:12:35,760
- I regretted it. - Right.

346
00:12:36,030 --> 00:12:37,230
- It was way too cold. - Yes.

347
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:40,799
- Was that the only time? - What?

348
00:12:40,800 --> 00:12:42,369
- Never mind. - That was the only time.

349
00:12:42,370 --> 00:12:43,399
- Really? - Yes.

350
00:12:43,400 --> 00:12:45,840
- You're the type to hold grudges. - Gosh, no.

351
00:12:46,240 --> 00:12:47,609
- That was the only time. - Really?

352
00:12:47,610 --> 00:12:49,010
- Don't get the wrong idea. - Okay.

353
00:12:49,070 --> 00:12:50,179
That's cute.

354
00:12:50,180 --> 00:12:51,240
(Laughing)

355
00:12:52,780 --> 00:12:55,909
(Panting)

356
00:12:55,910 --> 00:12:57,279
(Glancing)

357
00:12:57,280 --> 00:12:58,980
Hey, we're only 700m away.

358
00:12:59,450 --> 00:13:00,550
They're amazing.

359
00:13:00,720 --> 00:13:01,850
We've gotten far.

360
00:13:02,820 --> 00:13:04,740
- Let's take a break. - Yes, let's take a break.

361
00:13:06,830 --> 00:13:07,889
- Here. - Thank you.

362
00:13:07,890 --> 00:13:10,260
(Sitting down to hydrate)

363
00:13:11,600 --> 00:13:12,699
Drink some more.

364
00:13:12,700 --> 00:13:14,100
(Slurring)

365
00:13:15,400 --> 00:13:16,630
Gosh, the water tastes good.

366
00:13:17,970 --> 00:13:19,869
(Dripping)

367
00:13:19,870 --> 00:13:21,309
Water is dripping everywhere.

368
00:13:21,310 --> 00:13:22,839
(Laughing)

369
00:13:22,840 --> 00:13:23,979
You didn't feel the water dripping...

370
00:13:23,980 --> 00:13:25,479
- because your mouth was numb. - Right.

371
00:13:25,480 --> 00:13:27,880
The water actually felt warm.

372
00:13:28,450 --> 00:13:29,480
Right.

373
00:13:32,780 --> 00:13:35,349
(Of all days, )

374
00:13:35,350 --> 00:13:38,020
(why are we hiking today?)

375
00:13:38,960 --> 00:13:40,060
My gosh.

376
00:13:40,530 --> 00:13:42,490
- Should we go? - Yes, it's getting cold.

377
00:13:42,690 --> 00:13:45,360
- It's cold when we're not moving. - Yes. We need to keep moving.

378
00:13:45,760 --> 00:13:47,769
- Once our body cooled down... - Yes.

379
00:13:47,770 --> 00:13:49,730
- Right. We had to keep moving. - You'd get cold.

380
00:13:50,030 --> 00:13:51,170
Your sweat would cool off.

381
00:13:52,040 --> 00:13:53,940
(Panting)

382
00:13:54,240 --> 00:13:55,470
My gosh. Seriously.

383
00:13:55,910 --> 00:13:57,209
The sun is nowhere to be seen.

384
00:13:57,210 --> 00:13:58,840
Right. I don't see the sun at all.

385
00:14:00,350 --> 00:14:01,649
(Glancing back)

386
00:14:01,650 --> 00:14:04,220
Dowoon, look over there. It's getting red.

387
00:14:05,050 --> 00:14:06,179
This is cool.

388
00:14:06,180 --> 00:14:08,119
(Dowoon, look over there.)

389
00:14:08,120 --> 00:14:09,190
This is nice.

390
00:14:09,750 --> 00:14:10,959
(The scenery of Seoul is seen as they climb higher.)

391
00:14:10,960 --> 00:14:12,589
I'm starting to see Seoul now.

392
00:14:12,590 --> 00:14:14,670
(The scenery of Seoul is seen as they climb higher.)

393
00:14:15,660 --> 00:14:17,299
- It's like the view at the airport. - Yes.

394
00:14:17,300 --> 00:14:18,760
- Before landing. - Right.

395
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:20,369
- It's the view from the plane. - Right?

396
00:14:20,370 --> 00:14:21,776
- Yes. Right before landing. - The view at the airport.

397
00:14:21,800 --> 00:14:23,030
That's a cool spot.

398
00:14:25,300 --> 00:14:27,240
(Panting)

399
00:14:27,940 --> 00:14:29,670
What? Are we here?

400
00:14:31,440 --> 00:14:33,109
Hey, this is it.

401
00:14:33,110 --> 00:14:34,849
(They're finally at the peak.)

402
00:14:34,850 --> 00:14:35,909
We're at the peak.

403
00:14:35,910 --> 00:14:38,849
(They make it to the peak at last.)

404
00:14:38,850 --> 00:14:40,690
- You made it to Maebong Peak. - You made it.

405
00:14:40,990 --> 00:14:42,590
We made it, but it was so dark.

406
00:14:42,950 --> 00:14:44,060
Do you want a picture?

407
00:14:44,360 --> 00:14:46,641
- Let's take one together. - Yes. Let's take it together.

408
00:14:47,030 --> 00:14:49,129
Do you want to make a heart together?

409
00:14:49,130 --> 00:14:50,130
Let's make one.

410
00:14:50,131 --> 00:14:51,691
"Do you want to make a heart together?"

411
00:14:54,130 --> 00:14:57,740
(They're serious about taking pictures even when it's cold.)

412
00:14:58,600 --> 00:15:00,199
(Getting close)

413
00:15:00,200 --> 00:15:01,410
- Did we get it? - Yes.

414
00:15:03,270 --> 00:15:05,609
(Thanks for the good energy.)

415
00:15:05,610 --> 00:15:06,610
Come on.

416
00:15:06,810 --> 00:15:08,880
- This is scary. - It is.

417
00:15:09,380 --> 00:15:10,749
We can't even tell you apart.

418
00:15:10,750 --> 00:15:12,420
(Two unidentified hikers)

419
00:15:12,820 --> 00:15:14,449
- By the way, - That couldn't have been easy.

420
00:15:14,450 --> 00:15:17,189
I had never seen the peak being that empty.

421
00:15:17,190 --> 00:15:18,459
- Right. - Seriously.

422
00:15:18,460 --> 00:15:20,929
I went there 2 or 3 times. I had to line up to take a picture there.

423
00:15:20,930 --> 00:15:22,289
This mountain gets a lot of hikers usually.

424
00:15:22,290 --> 00:15:23,589
- Really? - Yes. It's a famous mountain.

425
00:15:23,590 --> 00:15:24,960
Especially in spring.

426
00:15:26,630 --> 00:15:31,300
(Current time, 6:55am)

427
00:15:31,670 --> 00:15:34,509
Oh, no. This is bad. The sun won't rise for another 40 minutes.

428
00:15:34,510 --> 00:15:35,840
(The sunrise time, 7:43am)

429
00:15:35,910 --> 00:15:38,679
The sign said that it would take...

430
00:15:38,680 --> 00:15:40,780
two hours to reach the peak.

431
00:15:41,610 --> 00:15:43,180
Maybe, it was for a round trip.

432
00:15:43,680 --> 00:15:45,279
Or maybe, we hiked quickly.

433
00:15:45,280 --> 00:15:47,619
It turned out we got there only in an hour and a half.

434
00:15:47,620 --> 00:15:50,149
We had to wait for 40 to 50 minutes until the sunrise.

435
00:15:50,150 --> 00:15:51,760
We got there too early.

436
00:15:51,990 --> 00:15:53,659
- Did you have to wait? - Yes.

437
00:15:53,660 --> 00:15:55,589
We could've slept for one more hour.

438
00:15:55,590 --> 00:15:57,229
You didn't get to look around while hiking.

439
00:15:57,230 --> 00:15:58,899
- So anyone would've gone up fast. - Right.

440
00:15:58,900 --> 00:16:00,129
You couldn't see anything around you.

441
00:16:00,130 --> 00:16:01,329
- So... - I see.

442
00:16:01,330 --> 00:16:02,369
- They just hiked up. - Yes.

443
00:16:02,370 --> 00:16:04,799
- Dowoon, to see the sunrise, - Yes.

444
00:16:04,800 --> 00:16:07,309
Let's go to Maebawi. Let's watch it from there.

445
00:16:07,310 --> 00:16:09,709
- We can't see the sun from here. - It's because of the trees.

446
00:16:09,710 --> 00:16:11,110
We'll get a better view there.

447
00:16:12,480 --> 00:16:13,809
You can't go higher from there?

448
00:16:13,810 --> 00:16:15,949
- No. - No. There's a rock...

449
00:16:15,950 --> 00:16:17,120
only 100m away.

450
00:16:18,720 --> 00:16:20,079
- Oh, there? - Yes.

451
00:16:20,080 --> 00:16:22,990
Okay. I see. This was one of the peaks.

452
00:16:23,550 --> 00:16:24,759
The view looks great from here.

453
00:16:24,760 --> 00:16:26,990
(They can see a panoramic view of the city.)

454
00:16:28,090 --> 00:16:29,090
There it is.

455
00:16:29,091 --> 00:16:31,330
(Grabbing)

456
00:16:32,060 --> 00:16:33,799
This helps us maintain our body temperature.

457
00:16:33,800 --> 00:16:34,830
What's that?

458
00:16:35,270 --> 00:16:37,239
- What is that? - Is it a hand warmer?

459
00:16:37,240 --> 00:16:38,640
(What's that?)

460
00:16:38,770 --> 00:16:41,239
- That's like silver foil. - Kian84. I brought this...

461
00:16:41,240 --> 00:16:42,939
- in case we got cold. - It's the emergency silver foil.

462
00:16:42,940 --> 00:16:44,079
It traps heat.

463
00:16:44,080 --> 00:16:45,916
(Dowoon brought a survival item, a silver-foil blanket.)

464
00:16:45,940 --> 00:16:47,109
- Like a sweatsuit? - Yes.

465
00:16:47,110 --> 00:16:49,010
- Heat can't escape. - Right.

466
00:16:49,150 --> 00:16:51,650
People wrap it around their body before the marathons.

467
00:16:52,150 --> 00:16:54,220
- That's right. - They take it off when they start.

468
00:16:54,820 --> 00:16:56,289
I doubt you packed it because you knew it'd be that cold.

469
00:16:56,290 --> 00:16:58,919
I packed it just in case.

470
00:16:58,920 --> 00:17:00,319
To be honest, I didn't think I'd use it.

471
00:17:00,320 --> 00:17:02,329
I'm so glad you packed it. That saved you both.

472
00:17:02,330 --> 00:17:04,630
I really didn't think I'd use it.

473
00:17:04,660 --> 00:17:06,636
- Do you have one? Okay. Get it. - I'll take out mine.

474
00:17:06,660 --> 00:17:08,030
(Shoving)

475
00:17:09,270 --> 00:17:10,899
- What are you doing? - Why?

476
00:17:10,900 --> 00:17:12,369
- My ears were way too cold. - I see. Your ears were cold.

477
00:17:12,370 --> 00:17:13,539
Hey, this is warm.

478
00:17:13,540 --> 00:17:15,109
Yes. It traps heat.

479
00:17:15,110 --> 00:17:16,169
Hey, this is amazing.

480
00:17:16,170 --> 00:17:17,240
- Really? - Yes.

481
00:17:17,480 --> 00:17:18,679
- Is it good? - Yes.

482
00:17:18,680 --> 00:17:19,809
I've never used it before.

483
00:17:19,810 --> 00:17:21,679
- Gosh, this is great. - It looks pretty cold.

484
00:17:21,680 --> 00:17:23,309
- But I guess it's not. - No.

485
00:17:23,310 --> 00:17:25,220
- It's for insulation. - I can sit on my bag.

486
00:17:25,720 --> 00:17:26,820
Gosh, it's freezing.

487
00:17:30,520 --> 00:17:31,619
The sky has gotten brighter.

488
00:17:31,620 --> 00:17:33,060
It's getting bright.

489
00:17:33,790 --> 00:17:35,460
I don't think we can see the sun.

490
00:17:35,860 --> 00:17:37,130
Are you sure we'll see the sun?

491
00:17:37,360 --> 00:17:38,930
(Checking)

492
00:17:39,160 --> 00:17:41,900
We need to wait for another 30 minutes.

493
00:17:42,470 --> 00:17:44,399
(It's only 7:10am now.)

494
00:17:44,400 --> 00:17:46,370
(Glancing)

495
00:17:48,040 --> 00:17:49,240
This is the one.

496
00:17:50,270 --> 00:17:51,909
(He takes another survival item from his backpack.)

497
00:17:51,910 --> 00:17:52,939
- Here. - Oh, that?

498
00:17:52,940 --> 00:17:54,550
- Yes. - Is it food?

499
00:17:55,650 --> 00:17:57,250
- Oh, great. - My gosh.

500
00:17:57,520 --> 00:17:58,979
You brought field ration. Gosh.

501
00:17:58,980 --> 00:18:00,179
- Let's have one. - It tastes amazing.

502
00:18:00,180 --> 00:18:01,619
- Of course. - He packed everything.

503
00:18:01,620 --> 00:18:03,190
"Yukgaejang flavored ramyeon rice."

504
00:18:03,220 --> 00:18:04,719
It heats up right away, right?

505
00:18:04,720 --> 00:18:05,760
Yes.

506
00:18:06,120 --> 00:18:07,890
- We just need to wait ten minutes. - Right.

507
00:18:08,090 --> 00:18:09,960
- Gosh. - My goodness.

508
00:18:10,630 --> 00:18:11,700
Hey.

509
00:18:13,630 --> 00:18:15,070
I'm too cold to make it.

510
00:18:16,400 --> 00:18:17,899
Hold on. Let me make it for you.

511
00:18:17,900 --> 00:18:19,339
No. Give it to me. I'll do it.

512
00:18:19,340 --> 00:18:21,070
Gosh, Kian84. Just sit tight.

513
00:18:21,540 --> 00:18:22,640
(Look at this guy.)

514
00:18:22,940 --> 00:18:24,179
How do you make this?

515
00:18:24,180 --> 00:18:25,209
(Trying to take care of each other)

516
00:18:25,210 --> 00:18:26,709
- You've never tried it, right? - No.

517
00:18:26,710 --> 00:18:28,450
I've made that many times.

518
00:18:29,010 --> 00:18:30,779
- "Then zip it up tightly." - Gosh.

519
00:18:30,780 --> 00:18:31,950
(Grabbing)

520
00:18:32,050 --> 00:18:33,990
- "Pour cold water..." - Hey, I'll do it.

521
00:18:34,320 --> 00:18:36,090
- Kian84 is so cool. - "The ramyeon rice..."

522
00:18:36,290 --> 00:18:37,959
Pour the water into this.

523
00:18:37,960 --> 00:18:39,466
(The older guy prepares the field ration.)

524
00:18:39,490 --> 00:18:41,050
- Is that all the water we have? - Yes.

525
00:18:41,130 --> 00:18:43,329
- We don't have more water? - That's all we have.

526
00:18:43,330 --> 00:18:44,999
- This is all the water we have? - That's it.

527
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:46,160
Hey, we can't make this then.

528
00:18:46,730 --> 00:18:48,170
We drank everything.

529
00:18:49,170 --> 00:18:50,839
(They drank up their precious water on their way up.)

530
00:18:50,840 --> 00:18:53,360
- You drank a lot of water here. - Gosh, the water tastes good.

531
00:18:53,440 --> 00:18:54,609
We need more water.

532
00:18:54,610 --> 00:18:55,850
(Using every drop of the water)

533
00:18:56,070 --> 00:18:57,840
- Let's try it. - Okay.

534
00:18:58,110 --> 00:18:59,279
- I'll zip it. - Zip it.

535
00:18:59,280 --> 00:19:00,780
- Gosh. - It's so cold.

536
00:19:01,180 --> 00:19:02,479
My hands are about to freeze off.

537
00:19:02,480 --> 00:19:04,080
(Their ears and hands might freeze off.)

538
00:19:05,280 --> 00:19:07,219
- How many minutes? - It was way too cold.

539
00:19:07,220 --> 00:19:08,980
- I couldn't keep my hands out. - Seriously.

540
00:19:09,720 --> 00:19:10,860
Have some.

541
00:19:11,860 --> 00:19:13,390
No, you should drink it. I'm okay.

542
00:19:13,660 --> 00:19:15,829
I made it for you this morning.

543
00:19:15,830 --> 00:19:18,260
- Really? Thank you. - Sure.

544
00:19:19,730 --> 00:19:21,430
- Really? - Yes.

545
00:19:22,930 --> 00:19:24,799
(Grateful)

546
00:19:24,800 --> 00:19:26,140
Let's split that together.

547
00:19:26,370 --> 00:19:28,139
Gosh, Kian84. It's hot. This is so good.

548
00:19:28,140 --> 00:19:30,180
- Kian84, you should have some. - It's good, right?

549
00:19:30,240 --> 00:19:32,440
- It must be nice to drink it there. - It was nice.

550
00:19:33,210 --> 00:19:34,250
Job's Tears tea?

551
00:19:35,850 --> 00:19:36,880
Job's Tears tea?

552
00:19:37,520 --> 00:19:38,780
- It's coffee. - Coffee?

553
00:19:39,820 --> 00:19:41,419
Your senses went numb.

554
00:19:41,420 --> 00:19:43,149
- It was too cold to taste anything. - That's coffee?

555
00:19:43,150 --> 00:19:45,120
- Right. Your tongue was numb. - It's coffee?

556
00:19:45,590 --> 00:19:46,819
My tongue is numb.

557
00:19:46,820 --> 00:19:48,490
My gosh. This is good.

558
00:19:49,630 --> 00:19:51,060
My hands are so cold.

559
00:19:52,100 --> 00:19:53,899
I'm afraid Kian84 might die at this rate.

560
00:19:53,900 --> 00:19:54,929
Seriously.

561
00:19:54,930 --> 00:19:57,199
We were tired too. It couldn't have gotten worse.

562
00:19:57,200 --> 00:19:58,600
(His face is freezing in the cold.)

563
00:19:59,500 --> 00:20:00,840
Kian84, wrap it around you.

564
00:20:01,440 --> 00:20:02,640
You should wrap it around you.

565
00:20:03,370 --> 00:20:05,140
I'll use mine.

566
00:20:05,440 --> 00:20:07,350
No, I'll do it for you. Sit tight.

567
00:20:08,450 --> 00:20:09,949
(The younger one puts a blanket around the older one.)

568
00:20:09,950 --> 00:20:12,050
- Like this. - How sweet.

569
00:20:12,620 --> 00:20:13,620
Yes.

570
00:20:13,720 --> 00:20:16,850
(Desperately trying to block out the wind with the survival item)

571
00:20:17,760 --> 00:20:19,019
(Shivering)

572
00:20:19,020 --> 00:20:20,860
It must've been really cold.

573
00:20:21,530 --> 00:20:24,460
(He makes sure Kian84 is okay first.)

574
00:20:24,960 --> 00:20:27,429
- Here it is. My gosh. - This is really warm.

575
00:20:27,430 --> 00:20:29,630
- Yes, Kian84. We need this. - This is really nice.

576
00:20:31,140 --> 00:20:32,940
I'm so glad I packed these.

577
00:20:34,470 --> 00:20:35,769
(Grateful)

578
00:20:35,770 --> 00:20:37,380
- This feels nice. - Yes.

579
00:20:38,940 --> 00:20:40,980
- You're wearing thin socks too. - Right.

580
00:20:41,650 --> 00:20:42,650
Right.

581
00:20:42,651 --> 00:20:44,750
(Exposed)

582
00:20:45,620 --> 00:20:46,880
My gosh.

583
00:20:47,120 --> 00:20:48,550
Look how red his ears are.

584
00:20:49,120 --> 00:20:50,620
His lips got pale.

585
00:20:52,520 --> 00:20:53,719
(Shaking)

586
00:20:53,720 --> 00:20:55,259
You're still shaking even with the blanket?

587
00:20:55,260 --> 00:20:56,629
It's really cold up there.

588
00:20:56,630 --> 00:20:57,999
- He's not moving now. - Yes.

589
00:20:58,000 --> 00:20:59,800
- Right. - It's colder with cool sweat.

590
00:21:01,900 --> 00:21:03,600
It looks like we went there to pray.

591
00:21:06,170 --> 00:21:08,910
(Two monks are sitting at the peak with fluttering blankets.)

592
00:21:09,440 --> 00:21:11,239
If the blankets get reflected by the sun,

593
00:21:11,240 --> 00:21:13,510
people will take pictures of you and think you're UFOs.

594
00:21:17,380 --> 00:21:18,549
I wanted to come down.

595
00:21:18,550 --> 00:21:20,149
(I wanted to give up on seeing the sunrise.)

596
00:21:20,150 --> 00:21:22,490
I just thought that...

597
00:21:23,350 --> 00:21:26,390
we wouldn't be able to last anymore.

598
00:21:26,460 --> 00:21:27,689
It was the toughest moment.

599
00:21:27,690 --> 00:21:29,129
(I want to be back in my warm house.)

600
00:21:29,130 --> 00:21:32,000
It felt like minus 20°C.

601
00:21:32,260 --> 00:21:34,170
- You should've covered your ears. - Right.

602
00:21:34,630 --> 00:21:36,169
I couldn't feel anything.

603
00:21:36,170 --> 00:21:39,169
When I touched my fingers, they felt like solid objects.

604
00:21:39,170 --> 00:21:40,639
My senses were numb.

605
00:21:40,640 --> 00:21:42,370
Right. Your senses would go numb.

606
00:21:43,110 --> 00:21:44,639
The North Pole is much warmer.

607
00:21:44,640 --> 00:21:46,310
Here's a message for those...

608
00:21:46,780 --> 00:21:49,680
who are not sure whether or not to visit the North Pole.

609
00:21:50,010 --> 00:21:51,780
The weather is about the same.

610
00:21:52,150 --> 00:21:54,449
When I went up, I kept slurring my words.

611
00:21:54,450 --> 00:21:56,390
I started to feel dizzy.

612
00:21:56,490 --> 00:21:58,560
I don't even remember what we talked about.

613
00:22:00,890 --> 00:22:03,060
Both of us look like beggars on the street.

614
00:22:05,430 --> 00:22:07,330
- By the way, it must be ready now. - What?

615
00:22:07,770 --> 00:22:10,070
That must be hot now.

616
00:22:11,200 --> 00:22:12,240
Hey, this looks great.

617
00:22:13,500 --> 00:22:15,769
(Steaming)

618
00:22:15,770 --> 00:22:17,040
That looks so good.

619
00:22:17,070 --> 00:22:18,340
- It looks amazing. - Yes.

620
00:22:18,710 --> 00:22:20,479
- It's ramyeon rice. - It's ramyeon rice?

621
00:22:20,480 --> 00:22:21,680
- Yes. - Rice.

622
00:22:22,980 --> 00:22:24,150
- Dowoon. - Yes?

623
00:22:24,280 --> 00:22:26,079
- Should I taste it first? - Go ahead.

624
00:22:26,080 --> 00:22:27,349
- Okay. - Have some first.

625
00:22:27,350 --> 00:22:29,420
- Then give me the bag. - Okay.

626
00:22:31,290 --> 00:22:35,130
(Shaking)

627
00:22:36,260 --> 00:22:37,900
Gosh, that looks great.

628
00:22:37,960 --> 00:22:38,960
(Humming)

629
00:22:38,961 --> 00:22:40,130
I want to know how it tastes.

630
00:22:40,930 --> 00:22:42,229
- There's rice too. - Yes.

631
00:22:42,230 --> 00:22:43,270
Right.

632
00:22:45,940 --> 00:22:46,940
(Slurping)

633
00:22:46,941 --> 00:22:49,510
(Inhaling the food without taking a breath)

634
00:22:50,070 --> 00:22:51,439
- Thank you. - Here.

635
00:22:51,440 --> 00:22:52,509
(Try a bite too.)

636
00:22:52,510 --> 00:22:53,540
It's the best.

637
00:22:54,080 --> 00:22:55,280
Gosh, it's so warm.

638
00:22:57,010 --> 00:22:59,720
(Nice. It's warm.)

639
00:23:00,420 --> 00:23:02,019
(Opening up his numb mouth)

640
00:23:02,020 --> 00:23:03,250
Hold on.

641
00:23:04,090 --> 00:23:05,859
I shouldn't laugh at this.

642
00:23:05,860 --> 00:23:07,060
(Finding him cute)

643
00:23:10,800 --> 00:23:13,030
(Enjoying it)

644
00:23:13,200 --> 00:23:14,830
- Gosh. - Isn't it good?

645
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:16,030
Oh, my.

646
00:23:16,570 --> 00:23:18,469
I didn't know he could change only in two hours.

647
00:23:18,470 --> 00:23:19,700
The field ration is the best.

648
00:23:20,500 --> 00:23:21,669
(Eating in a hurry)

649
00:23:21,670 --> 00:23:24,109
Yes. Ramyeon after suffering like that...

650
00:23:24,110 --> 00:23:26,110
- Yes. It tasted so different. - tastes different.

651
00:23:26,310 --> 00:23:28,126
Kian84, put your hand on the bottom of the bag.

652
00:23:28,150 --> 00:23:29,710
- It's warm. - Okay.

653
00:23:30,680 --> 00:23:32,560
- It will warm up your hand. - Gosh, it's warm.

654
00:23:33,120 --> 00:23:35,750
(Gosh, it's warm.)

655
00:23:37,720 --> 00:23:38,760
(Slurping)

656
00:23:39,560 --> 00:23:41,730
Kian84. Gosh, what are we? Beggars on the street?

657
00:23:42,090 --> 00:23:43,430
(Sniffling)

658
00:23:43,830 --> 00:23:45,200
I should try the soup too.

659
00:23:47,300 --> 00:23:48,870
(Blowing)

660
00:23:50,100 --> 00:23:52,069
(Thoroughly enjoying the warm soup)

661
00:23:52,070 --> 00:23:53,270
Gosh, the soup...

662
00:23:53,600 --> 00:23:54,740
I bet it tastes so good.

663
00:23:55,740 --> 00:23:57,270
Dowoon, try the soup.

664
00:23:57,880 --> 00:24:00,110
- The soup was great. - We had to take turns like that.

665
00:24:00,280 --> 00:24:02,710
It'd be too cold to keep our hands out at the same time.

666
00:24:05,020 --> 00:24:06,519
(Shaking)

667
00:24:06,520 --> 00:24:08,449
- This is just crazy. - My gosh.

668
00:24:08,450 --> 00:24:09,590
(Shaking)

669
00:24:10,420 --> 00:24:11,720
That's just pure misery.

670
00:24:12,260 --> 00:24:14,330
Why did you guys go hiking that day?

671
00:24:14,560 --> 00:24:16,760
Did you have to look at the sunrise that day?

672
00:24:16,890 --> 00:24:18,536
You should've looked at it on another day.

673
00:24:18,560 --> 00:24:19,630
- Another day? - You know?

674
00:24:19,900 --> 00:24:21,900
You might be too busy eating and miss the sunrise.

675
00:24:22,830 --> 00:24:23,869
Right?

676
00:24:23,870 --> 00:24:25,370
Is the sun already up?

677
00:24:25,500 --> 00:24:27,469
- Seriously. - Dowoon plays the drums.

678
00:24:27,470 --> 00:24:29,710
His forearm muscles must be really strong.

679
00:24:29,840 --> 00:24:31,179
It must've been really cold for his arms...

680
00:24:31,180 --> 00:24:32,879
- to shake. You know? - Nothing can beat the cold waves.

681
00:24:32,880 --> 00:24:33,909
Seriously.

682
00:24:33,910 --> 00:24:35,790
(Thinking about it still gives him the chills.)

683
00:24:35,910 --> 00:24:37,950
(It's nice to have warm ramyeon, though.)

684
00:24:38,680 --> 00:24:40,950
(Finishing up)

685
00:24:42,450 --> 00:24:44,320
Hold on. Let me bundle up.

686
00:24:46,360 --> 00:24:48,490
(Wrapping himself)

687
00:24:52,030 --> 00:24:54,269
- The sun will rise from there! - What?

688
00:24:54,270 --> 00:24:55,700
I think it'll rise from there.

689
00:24:56,000 --> 00:24:58,470
The sun rose! It already rose, right?

690
00:24:58,900 --> 00:25:00,599
- You need to see the egg. - The egg?

691
00:25:00,600 --> 00:25:02,009
- The yolk? - The white circle.

692
00:25:02,010 --> 00:25:04,139
It's cloudy. They won't see it.

693
00:25:04,140 --> 00:25:05,680
It's a bit nerve-racking, right?

694
00:25:06,480 --> 00:25:07,509
I think the sun rose.

695
00:25:07,510 --> 00:25:09,409
- That's... - I'll need to look it up.

696
00:25:09,410 --> 00:25:10,980
(I'll need to look it up.)

697
00:25:11,550 --> 00:25:14,150
It's the time of sunrise,

698
00:25:14,750 --> 00:25:15,990
but because of those clouds...

699
00:25:16,290 --> 00:25:17,990
I'll ask ChatGPT.

700
00:25:18,920 --> 00:25:21,160
(Really?)

701
00:25:22,130 --> 00:25:23,929
(AI84 is the best at utilizing AI.)

702
00:25:23,930 --> 00:25:26,030
- Do you use it as well? - Of course.

703
00:25:28,330 --> 00:25:31,670
I'm at Maebong, the summit of Mount Cheonggye...

704
00:25:32,040 --> 00:25:33,539
right now.

705
00:25:33,540 --> 00:25:34,770
Did the sun rise?

706
00:25:35,240 --> 00:25:37,880
You went all the way up to Maebong, the summit of Mount Cheonggye.

707
00:25:38,210 --> 00:25:40,079
You're curious about whether or not the sun rose, right?

708
00:25:40,080 --> 00:25:42,480
It's around the time of sunrise.

709
00:25:42,610 --> 00:25:44,519
Seeing the sun rise at the summit of a mountain...

710
00:25:44,520 --> 00:25:46,319
will surely be nice.

711
00:25:46,320 --> 00:25:49,050
Hey, we're asking if it rose!

712
00:25:50,120 --> 00:25:52,990
I see. You want to know if it has risen already, right?

713
00:25:53,260 --> 00:25:55,290
- I'm pretty sure... - Just answer without asking!

714
00:25:56,590 --> 00:25:59,330
- The AI kept using flowery words. - I'm pretty sure it has risen.

715
00:25:59,530 --> 00:26:01,230
- Give me that. - Okay.

716
00:26:02,570 --> 00:26:05,370
When will we see the egg?

717
00:26:06,340 --> 00:26:09,639
By my estimation, the clouds will part...

718
00:26:09,640 --> 00:26:11,209
- in an hour or two... - In an hour or two,

719
00:26:11,210 --> 00:26:12,409
- and you'll see the sun. - it'll be high up in the sky.

720
00:26:12,410 --> 00:26:13,609
Will it take an hour or two?

721
00:26:13,610 --> 00:26:15,809
Of course. If you wait...

722
00:26:15,810 --> 00:26:17,049
(Stopping)

723
00:26:17,050 --> 00:26:18,880
It doesn't know.

724
00:26:19,580 --> 00:26:22,749
The AI technology isn't accurate yet.

725
00:26:22,750 --> 00:26:25,189
I bet swear words are the data AI collects the most.

726
00:26:25,190 --> 00:26:26,190
That's right.

727
00:26:26,960 --> 00:26:28,389
- Is that the sun? - That's the sun.

728
00:26:28,390 --> 00:26:30,359
If it goes up a bit more...

729
00:26:30,360 --> 00:26:32,120
- I think the sun has risen. - It has risen.

730
00:26:32,430 --> 00:26:35,929
It'll have to go up much further for us to see it.

731
00:26:35,930 --> 00:26:37,600
It'll need to go up further, right?

732
00:26:38,900 --> 00:26:40,970
(Let's see.)

733
00:26:44,610 --> 00:26:45,640
Dowoon.

734
00:26:45,740 --> 00:26:48,079
Let's just get rid of preconception...

735
00:26:48,080 --> 00:26:49,349
that the sun is round!

736
00:26:49,350 --> 00:26:50,809
- Exactly. - You see it, right?

737
00:26:50,810 --> 00:26:53,210
(Let's just get rid of preconception that the sun is round!)

738
00:26:53,380 --> 00:26:54,590
- It has risen. - Yes.

739
00:26:55,090 --> 00:26:56,149
Shall we make a wish?

740
00:26:56,150 --> 00:26:58,719
You can pray to Buddha and I can pray to the Almighty.

741
00:26:58,720 --> 00:27:00,619
- Okay. Let's make a wish. - They're an optimistic duo.

742
00:27:00,620 --> 00:27:02,530
- I love it. - Let's make a wish.

743
00:27:02,930 --> 00:27:04,700
You guys are brighter than the sun.

744
00:27:06,130 --> 00:27:07,200
It's cool.

745
00:27:08,830 --> 00:27:10,670
- Amen! - Gosh, Buddha.

746
00:27:12,000 --> 00:27:13,239
Homage to Amitabha Buddha.

747
00:27:13,240 --> 00:27:15,740
(Homage to Amitabha Buddha.)

748
00:27:17,570 --> 00:27:19,540
- We have different religions. - Religions.

749
00:27:19,680 --> 00:27:21,109
They'll be confused about...

750
00:27:21,110 --> 00:27:22,909
- They're so different. - whom to listen to.

751
00:27:22,910 --> 00:27:24,349
I bet they're close up there.

752
00:27:24,350 --> 00:27:26,049
Buddha will look after us.

753
00:27:26,050 --> 00:27:27,050
That's right.

754
00:27:27,051 --> 00:27:29,019
The Almighty will watch over us.

755
00:27:29,020 --> 00:27:32,320
(Buddhism and Christianity are in one place.)

756
00:27:32,990 --> 00:27:35,360
We prayed to our respective religious power.

757
00:27:35,990 --> 00:27:37,230
I just wished...

758
00:27:37,430 --> 00:27:39,430
that my parents would be healthy...

759
00:27:40,000 --> 00:27:42,830
and that I'd be a good person to those around me.

760
00:27:43,130 --> 00:27:44,500
I hoped that the round sun...

761
00:27:45,070 --> 00:27:46,199
(Ta-da)

762
00:27:46,200 --> 00:27:47,870
would come up like this.

763
00:27:48,070 --> 00:27:51,339
But we did see the sun that was pretty round.

764
00:27:51,340 --> 00:27:52,539
(Perhaps it was the sun of harmony.)

765
00:27:52,540 --> 00:27:53,840
- Amen. - Amen.

766
00:27:54,080 --> 00:27:55,250
Amen.

767
00:27:56,180 --> 00:27:57,409
I ended up saying it.

768
00:27:57,410 --> 00:27:59,380
- I got affected. - That was the vibe.

769
00:27:59,820 --> 00:28:02,520
I always have this thought at the summit of a mountain.

770
00:28:02,790 --> 00:28:06,860
"What was the use of all that squabbling in life?"

771
00:28:07,360 --> 00:28:09,559
Up there, everything you see is the size of an ant.

772
00:28:09,560 --> 00:28:10,830
It's like Buddhist TV.

773
00:28:11,530 --> 00:28:13,000
I don't wish for something big.

774
00:28:14,060 --> 00:28:16,900
I wish to continue being grateful for the things I have now.

775
00:28:17,840 --> 00:28:18,970
Seriously,

776
00:28:20,000 --> 00:28:22,710
I talk like my mom.

777
00:28:25,040 --> 00:28:26,279
(Although their religions differ, they are of one mind.)

778
00:28:26,280 --> 00:28:27,310
Amen.

779
00:28:27,880 --> 00:28:31,479
(They fully charge the New Year energy.)

780
00:28:31,480 --> 00:28:33,419
